        "type": "MCQ",
        "subject": "Biology",
        "chapter": "Biotechnology: Principles and Processes",
        "solution": "<p>The selectable markers of a cloning vector are antibiotic-resistance genes (e.g. for ampicillin or tetracycline), not the antibiotics themselves.</p> <p>Antibiotics are added to the medium so that only cells carrying the resistance gene can grow; non-transformed and contaminating bacteria are killed, i.e. the antibiotic keeps the medium free of unwanted bacteria.</p> <p>Antibiotics do not detect alien DNA (that is done by insertional inactivation or probes) and do not make the host plant disease-resistant.</p>"
