        "solution": "<p>Agrobacterium tumefaciens naturally transfers part of its Ti plasmid (the T-DNA) into dicot plant cells, causing crown gall.</p> <p>With its tumour-forming genes removed, the Ti plasmid becomes a harmless vector that can carry desired genes into many kinds of plants; the Ri plasmid of A. rhizogenes is used in the same way.</p> <p>So the plant vector is obtained from Agrobacterium spp.</p>"
