        "solution": "<p>Treating bacteria with divalent Ca2+ ions (then heat shock) makes them competent to take up rDNA, so that statement is true.</p> <p>E. coli and Agrobacterium tumefaciens are the organisms used for cloning in plant biotechnology, which is also true.</p> <p>Uptake of naked DNA by a cell is transformation; transduction is gene transfer by a bacteriophage, so that statement is wrong.</p> <p>A cell that has taken up the rDNA is called a transformed (recombinant) cell, which is true.</p> <p>So the incorrect statement is the one calling uptake of naked rDNA transduction.</p>"
