        "solution": "<p>Statement (I) is true: transformation is inefficient, so only some host cells take up the recombinant DNA, giving a mixture of transformed and untransformed cells.</p> <p>Statement (II) is false: screening uses a selectable marker (e.g. antibiotic resistance) so that only transformed cells survive and multiply.</p> <p>The division of host cells along with replication of the recombinant DNA describes amplification of the selected transformed cells, not of both types.</p> <p>Hence the first statement is right and the second is wrong.</p>"
