        "solution": "<p>The correct answer is: </p> <p>✅ <strong>Option B – PCR (Polymerase Chain Reaction)</strong> </p> <p><strong>Explanation:</strong> </p> <ul> <li><p><strong>PCR</strong> is a molecular biology technique used for <em>in vitro</em> amplification (copying) of a specific gene or DNA segment. It allows the creation of millions of copies of a particular DNA sequence within a few hours. </p></li> <li><p><strong>Electrophoresis</strong>, <strong>PAGE (Polyacrylamide Gel Electrophoresis)</strong>, and <strong>SDS-PAGE</strong> are analytical techniques used to <em>separate</em> nucleic acids or proteins based on size and charge — not to amplify them. </p></li> </ul> <p><strong>Answer:</strong> <strong>B. PCR</strong></p>"
