        "solution": "<p>Assertion is true: human genes such as those for insulin or growth hormone are commonly cloned and expressed in hosts like <i>E. coli</i> or yeast.</p> <p>Reason is true: these microbes divide very rapidly and are easy to culture, so a single transformed cell soon gives a huge population that makes the desired product in quantity.</p> <p>This is exactly why they are chosen as hosts, so the Reason explains the Assertion.</p>"
