        "solution": "<p>Plasmids are small circular extra-chromosomal DNA molecules that replicate on their own, because each has its own origin of replication (ori).</p> <p>The ori controls how many copies are made, so a gene joined to a plasmid is copied along with it. The copy number can be raised artificially to clone the gene in large amounts.</p> <p>Antibiotic-resistance genes are useful only as selectable markers. They are not what lets a plasmid carry and multiply a gene.</p>"
