        "solution": "<p>Pst I recognises the palindromic sequence 5′3′ , which reads the same on both strands in the 5′→3′ direction, and cuts each strand between A and G, as the arrows show.</p> <p>The upper strand is cut between A and G, giving 5′ and 3′ .</p> <p>The lower strand, 3′5′ , is cut between G and A, giving 3′ and 5′ .</p> <p>Therefore the left fragment carries 5′ paired with 3′ , and the right fragment carries 3′ paired with 5′ , each with a single-stranded sticky end of four bases.</p> <p>Hence, the correct option is (D).</p>"
