        "solution": "<p>Cohen and Boyer in 1972 constructed the first recombinant DNA by linking an antibiotic resistance gene with a plasmid of <em>Salmonella typhimurium</em> and propagated it in <em>Escherichia coli</em>, using the host's DNA polymerase for replication.</p> <p><em>Thermus aquaticus</em> is the source of Taq polymerase used in PCR, not of the enzyme used in this work.</p> <p>Hence, the correct option is (C).</p>"
